--
-- Thalidomide's two forms invert at a measured half-life in human serum of 22 minutes from the (S) form
-- and 33 from the (R), at pH 7.4 and 37 C (td-inv above). The (S) form is the teratogen. So administering
-- the (R) form alone is not administering a substance whose hazard is the (R) form's hazard: within an hour
-- the body holds both.
--
-- the hazard of a pure form, as the record carries it: 1 for the form that does the harm, 0 for the other
form-hazard : Nat → Nat
form-hazard f = case eqb f 0 of true → 1; false → 0
